                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I cannot recommend the game in its current state.\n\nThe dialogue while manageable to piece together is poorly translated and is formatted as a wall of text that will really test your dyslexia. There's also some obtuse clichés and a few weirdly lecherous dialogue choices? I'm sure that it reads much better in the original Russian.\n\nThe main way to make money in the game reliably is to fill out \"reports\" which consists of waiting approximately 10 real-life minutes watching Chinese characters fill up a computer screen before you get the opportunity to collect a whopping $15 if you manage to click the button for it within 3 seconds of finishing.\n\nThe two forms of combat which make up the bulk of the main gameplay are also mechanically atrocious:\n\nThe first is you controlling Matthew on an isometric view where your mouse (barely) aims where your bullets will go vaguely in the direction you last clicked, but due to the isometric nature of the physics this is frequently wildly off. You have at most 15 degrees of precision to work with in any direction while attempting to crawl away from baddies at a snail's pace to reload, which makes you stationary and vulnerable to attacks. Stock up on beer and cigarettes.\n\nThe second is you playing Whack-A-Mole with grey figures that are either a screaming woman or an armed baddie which isn't so bad, except for the fact that your gun in the early game does not often have enough bullets to kill all of the baddies on screen, and that even if you MASH the R key Matthew will not reliably reload because the game has no frame cap which causes physics bugs.\n\nI'm fine with the driving for the most part, except the car is SLOW even at max speed, and turns are much slower. Also you're often facing the wrong direction to path to your destination efficiently, so doubling back on the street grid takes extra time.\n\nI feel like some help with the translations, an improved movement/combat physics scheme (bullets that actually travel in the direction you aim???), and graphics settings that allow for a framerate cap (so you don't have skipped frame physics bugs) would go a long way towards making this game much improved.",
